WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.920
Hey guys, how's it going

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:05.440
So apparently you all really liked that last insights video

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.000
It got a really good response and it did really well

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.040
So thanks for clicking on the like button and all that stuff

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.660
I figured, let's do one more, why not

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.500
Whenever I finish a video, I have all these facts and insights left over

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.580
That couldn't quite fit into it, so it feels good to give them a little home here.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.340
We start in the chalice dungeons this time

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.560
There's some really weird stuff down here, especially in the deepest depths

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.380
How many of you have seen this thing before?

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.500
It's listed as a "labyrinth mole" in the wiki

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.360
And, statistically, it has to be the rarest creature you can find in Bloodborne

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.060
It's not even listed in the official guide, that's how rare it is.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.720
It spits poisonous goop at you,  it slaps you around with its tentacles,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.800
It can move its head to either sides of its body,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.260
And well, obviously it has a grab attack.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.980
and I'm not surprised my character went a little bit insane from that one.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.880
Anyway, in the description below I've sourced its discovery

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.260
and you can come and gawk at it if you want.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.300
And it's funny, people come to this chalice dungeon

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.660
like they would go to look at an animal in a zoo.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.080
When I was walking up to it, there were all manner of messages like:

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.520
"Have audience with secret," or "Despicable blobby thing ahead"

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:21.000
Everyone just comes here to look at this thing, but don't kill it. "Treat blobby thing with care."

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.280
See if you can find my message here.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.560
And, did you know, speaking of messages

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:29.920
Good segue, did you know that if you rate messages as "fine" or "foul"

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.180
Then the messengers will react.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.380
They do a little dance when you rate it as fine,

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.760
and they cry when you rate it foul.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.760
Sometimes, when you go down a significant path in a Chalice Dungeon or in the Nighmare Realm

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.200
You might catch these little blue lantern guys in the corner

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:50.920
They're actually little proximity sensors that light their lantern so you know that you've been through here before

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.000
They're a little method to stop you getting lost that I discovered about a week ago, so.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.360
Really useful. Another thing you might have noticed on your Chalice Dungeon adventures

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:02.180
are the knights wearing plate.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.900
Since there are no plate-wearing knights in Bloodborne's overworld,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:09.340
It makes you wonder what era these knights were from.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:13.520
In my headcanon, maybe the first forays down into the Chalice Dungeons

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:17.580
were from a time long ago when plate was still popular.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:20.720
And then, finally, when they discovered what they were up against,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.820
The more experienced forays down into the Chalice Dungeons would have had

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.060
The lightweight attire that Gehrman used as a hunter, hunting the beasts,

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.380
because it says in his item description that he popularized it.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.140
Go through enough rooms, and eventually you'll find one with a giant bell in it

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.640
And of course, you're going to ring this thing, right?

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.040
You have to, how could you not?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:47.440
It's a mistake. When you do, what seems like every enemy in the bloody chalice dungeon will come

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.440
to find you and murder you.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:54.660
One of the most interesting things with this bell is that you can actually use the music box item

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:58.620
anywhere near the bell, and the bell will resonate as if it was hit.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.360
I've been trying this music box on everything lately

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:06.800
Eldritch, super hidden meanings aside, I guess what's happening here is the bell is set

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:12.560
as an inter-actable element of the world, and that the music box checks everything in its vicinity

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.780
to elicit a response from it and I guess that triggers the bell

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.600
And that's exactly what makes the music box interesting

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.980
It actually has more effects than you would have first thought.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:31.300
Everyone knows that Gascoigne reacts to the music box in the boss fight since it reminds him of his wife and daughters

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.980
But did you know that he also chuckles when you first play it near him

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.240
while he's summoned?

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.140
The song itself is the first few notes of "Mergo's Lullaby"

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.540
which plays during the Wet Nurse fight.

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:50.120
What's sort of interesting is that sometimes, if you spam this music box in this fight

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:54.100
it gets the boss caught in this endless cycle of side-stepping,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:58.060
Which is really curious. I read about this on the wiki and I had to give it a go.

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:04.380
Maybe it's reacting to the tune? So far as I know it's the only creature that does this sometimes

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.060
I do wonder if it's a bug, though, similar to with the giant bell.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:13.320
The idea that NPCs react to things that you do, other than attacks and talking,

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.560
Is something I hope they put into future games.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.860
Take the doll, for example. A lot of you probably realized

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.400
that she reponds to gestures, there's no great discovery here

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:27.740
She'll clap with you when you're excited, she bows back at you, and she tilts her head quizically

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.680
When you do something weird, it's so endearing.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.640
My favorite is when you do the "Make Contact" gesture

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:38.320
and this is the gesture that's used as some sort of communication with the great ones.

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:44.860
Wait a minute, and when your character switches sides, she all of a sudden decides to clap.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.860
Maybe she's impressed that you can do it correctly.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:51.320
And it turns out doing it correctly matters.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:56.660
If you "Make Contact" with the Brain of Mensis until your arms switch sides

00:04:56.660 --> 00:05:04.660
then you get the fully upgraded moon rune, which is the one that gives you more blood echoes.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.980
And this is the rune that also mentions that the great ones are sympathetic in spirit

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.920
which is appropriate. The Nightmare of Mensis building

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.120
is one of those places that's able to be seen from

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.360
the Nightmare Frontier. And I love little details like these.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:22.680
It makes you feel a little bit like you're exploring a real world.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:25.080
Bloodborne does it fairly convincingly.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:30.880
Other areas I've noticed are that Castle Cainhurst can be seen from Hemwick Charnel Lane

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:35.460
and you can also see the observatory at Byrgenwerth from the Forbidden Forest.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:39.640
Are there any I'm missing? You can let me know in the comments. I probably am missing some.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:43.000
The tenth little insight is to do with the beast roar.

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:45.500
Just like all the force spells in previous games,

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.140
Beast Roar deflects projectiles.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:54.500
Whether it be giant boulders, fireballs, bullets, you name it. Just roar them away.

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:58.360
Number eleven: did you know that there's a hidden exit when you're riding up

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:01.460
the Cathedral Ward elevator? I didn't until recently.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:08.380
It leads to the top floor of the Cathedral Ward, which houses the Formless Oedon rune and the urn costume

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.160
for the messengers. It also lets you do this.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.360
Number 12 takes us to the abandoned hunter's workshop.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:18.960
If you position yourself here, you hear something strange.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.640
(female vocalizing)

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:31.340
It's the sound of an old woman laughing, repeating the same sound over and over again.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:35.620
We've actually tracked down this sound to a door in an alleyway

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.620
in Cathedral Ward.

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:55.980
And it's a bizarre glitch, to say the least. It's so weird that a voice file would just start playing here,

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:59.960
and it's especially weird because this is a voice file that's located at the end

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:02.180
of one character's line of dialogue.

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:05.660
And it's not the full voice file. It's very strange.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.000
But, sometimes in Bloodborne, things are in the game without too much purpose.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.000
Take the Ring of Betrothal item for example.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:16.620
You find it in the Pthumeru Ihyll root chalice dungeon

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.420
and you can use it to propose to Annalise, the Vileblood queen.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.260
Even with all the hard work that you do for her, you still get rejected.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:27.700
And it turns out you're doing some pretty gross stuff for her.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:33.540
Annalise enlists hunters who go out and hunt other hunters so you can get their blood dregs

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:35.540
and feed them to your queen.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:41.900
And she consumes these so that she can, and I quote, "One day bear a child of blood."

00:07:42.240 --> 00:07:45.900
But have you ever looked closely at what the blood dregs are?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.400
When you do, it makes sense why they might help her bear a "child of blood."

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:52.980
They're clearly meant to resemble sperm.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:58.680
Maybe in the DLC there will be a use for that ring, but so far there's nothing that's been found.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:04.440
Another item like this is the Yharnam Stone, which you get when you kill Queen Yharnam in the chalice dungeon.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:11.920
It reads: "The queen lies dead, but her horrific consciousness is only asleep, and it stirs in unsettling motions."

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:16.800
The Yharnam Stone implies that the queen lives on, whether inside this stone

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.280
or in the Nightmare Realm, perhaps.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:23.780
It reminds me entirely of Annalise, Queen of the Vilebloods.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:28.900
Since she's the only other character who is immortal, and she's capable of living on

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.460
in a lump of flesh. And, make no mistake,

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:34.800
there are actually a lot of connections between these two characters.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.600
I was really excited about this when I discovered it around the time I was doing

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:43.280
the Cainhurst lore video, uh, but none of this information really fit in that video

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:46.780
because it does take a while to explain, but bear with me

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.720
Even the song that plays during Yharnam's boss fight

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:55.620
is titled "Queen of the Vilebloods" which is the same song that plays when you fight Logarius

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:58.740
who guards the actual queen of the Vilebloods.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.640
So, let's list some of the connections. There are two undying queens,

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.520
who leave behind a bloody token of their immortality.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:12.260
These are two queens that share the "Queen of the Vilebloods" soundtrack.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.420
They're also two queens with strong connections to blood.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:20.580
One of them started a line of followers who partook of her blood, that's Annalise,

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:25.260
and the other one wields a kind of blood sorcery when she fights.

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:31.740
Both of them are also related to the ring of betrothal, which is a ring found in Pthumeru Ihyll

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.600
which is also Queen Yharnam's chalice dungeon.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.380
And the description of the ring clearly relates to Queen Yharnam.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:43.560
And Queen Annalise is the only character who recognizes this ring as a wedding ring.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:49.120
A wedding ring that says it's only permitted to those who are slated to bear a special child,

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.340
which is a phrase that applies to both queens.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.580
So, I just rambled on quickly about their similarities,

00:09:55.580 --> 00:10:00.180
But what does this mean? What are some of the consequences for Bloodborne's timeline,

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.320
for example. Well, Vileblood, as mentioned by Alfred,

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:08.780
was another strain of the old blood, stolen from Byrgenwerth long ago

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:11.960
by a scholar. And this was likely back when

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.260
the scholars were still exploring the tombs.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:18.840
It makes you wonder: could Queen Yharnam be the source of this vileblood?

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:25.760
The thing that seals it for me is the fact that Queen Yharnam of the chalice dungeons has chains around her wrists

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:30.260
implying that she was perhaps found and restrained at some point

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:34.320
and maybe even exploited so that the blood could be taken from her.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:40.500
And it could have got into the populace and eventually led to the rise of the Vileblood line.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:45.940
Also, finally, when you hit Queen Yharnam, the baby Mergo screams out.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:51.880
She's clearly had something ripped from her pregnant stomach, perhaps it was the umbilical cord

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.800
that granted Mensis audience with Mergo, the infant great one

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.900
at the top of the Nightmare of Mensis.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:03.180
This would also explain Queen Yharnam's presence outside, after all. There are just so many

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:07.160
connections here, between Queen Yharnam and the outside world.

00:11:07.260 --> 00:11:09.520
So I'm curious to see what you guys think.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.740
Maybe we can take this a little bit further, even.

00:11:12.720 --> 00:11:16.860
And I think this is all I can think of. I don't think I'll be able to scrape together

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:21.380
another 15 things that are high enough in quality to include, so

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.380
Thanks so much for supporting this series,

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:27.760
and I hope you stay tuned for more Bloodborne and Dark Souls III stuff in the future

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:30.640
And I'll see you in the next one. Cheers guys.

